issues.body:
## Problem
The bank list is fixed at build time: `packages/core/src/vietqr/banks.ts` loads `packages/core/data/banks.json` into `BANKS` and builds the `byBin` / `byCode` maps once at module load. `findBank`, `searchBanks`, `buildVietQR` and `parseVietQR` only see those entries.

Users who need a bank or wallet that the bundled list lacks, or has under an old name, have no way to supply it. Examples raised in #203 are Vikki, Vietcombank Neo and ZaloPay. #203 stays blocked until a maintainer picks an official source, so these users have no workaround. Competitor `@viet-qr/core` 1.4.0 offers `setBankList([...])` (https://unpkg.com/@viet-qr/core/README.md).

The data comes from the caller, so vn-skills itself asserts no new bank facts. The bundled `banks.json` stays unchanged.

## Proposed surface
- Core, in `packages/core/src/vietqr/banks.ts`, exported from `vietqr/index.ts`:
  - `registerBanks(entries: Bank[], options?: { mode?: 'merge' | 'replace' }): Result<{ count: number; added: string[]; replaced: string[] }>`
  - `merge` (default): an entry whose BIN matches a bundled bank replaces that bank; any other entry is added.
  - `replace`: the given entries become the whole list.
  - `resetBanks()`: restores the bundled list.
- Validation is atomic: if any entry is invalid, nothing changes and the result is `ok:false` with code `INVALID_BANKS`. The message lists each bad entry by index and reason. An entry is valid when:
  - `bin` is 6 digits, matching the `Bank` type doc;
  - `code`, `shortName` and `name` are non-empty strings;
  - `swift`, if given, is 8 or 11 alphanumeric characters;
  - `vietqr`, if given, is one of the existing union values;
  - no BIN or code (case-insensitive) is duplicated within the entries or against the remaining registry.
- `findBank`, `searchBanks`, the SWIFT lookup, `buildVietQR` and `parseVietQR` read the current registry. Rebuild the lookup maps on register and reset. Keep the `BANKS` export as the bundled list and add `listBanks()`, which returns the current registry.
- Offline only: no fetch, no URLs; entries come from the caller.
- CLI: global option or per-command `--banks <file.json>` on `vietqr build`, `vietqr parse`, `vietqr decode` and `vietqr banks`. It reads a JSON array of entries and calls `registerBanks` in merge mode. Errors are JSON in `--json` mode (`READ_ERROR`, `INVALID_BANKS`).
- MCP: `packages/mcp/src/index.ts` accepts `--banks <file.json>` in both stdio and `--http` mode and registers the entries before the server starts. An invalid file prints the error to stderr and exits with status 1.

## Acceptance
- [ ] `registerBanks`, `resetBanks` and `listBanks` are exported from `@vn-skills/core`.
- [ ] ≥ 20 tests in `tests/vietqr-banks-registry.test.ts`, covering:
  - merge adding a new BIN;
  - merge overriding a bundled BIN's name and code;
  - replace mode;
  - a duplicate BIN, a duplicate code and an invalid BIN, each rejected with the registry unchanged;
  - `resetBanks`;
  - `findBank` by the new code and by a keyword;
  - a build → parse round trip with a custom BIN that resolves to the custom name;
  - CLI `--banks` on build and parse;
  - the MCP server started with `--banks` returning the custom bank from `vietqr_banks`.
- [ ] Tests call `resetBanks()` in `afterEach` so the global registry does not leak between tests.
- [ ] `skills/vietqr/SKILL.md`, `README.md` and `README.vi.md` document `--banks`, with a note that vn-skills does not verify user-supplied entries.
- [ ] `pnpm build && pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm exec vitest run && pnpm format:check` pass.

