issues.body:
## Problem
Retail and POS prices are usually quoted with VAT included, so people need questions like "Giá 1.080.000 đã gồm VAT 8%, tiền hàng và thuế là bao nhiêu?" answered.

`computeTotals` in `packages/core/src/einvoice/totals.ts` only works forward: net amount × `vatPercent(rate)`, rounded with `roundVnd`. Nothing works backwards from a gross price. Agents therefore do the division themselves and may round differently from `computeTotals`.

## Proposed surface
- Core, in `packages/core/src/einvoice/vat.ts`, exported from `einvoice/index.ts`:
  - `splitVatInclusive(gross: number, vatRate: VatRate): Result<{ gross; net; vat; rate }>`
    - `net = roundVnd(gross * 100 / (100 + vatPercent(rate)))` and `vat = gross - net`, so `net + vat === gross` always.
    - For `0`, `'KCT'` and `'KKKNT'`, net equals gross and VAT is 0, as `vatPercent` already gives.
  - `applyVat(net: number, vatRate: VatRate): Result<{ net; vat; gross; rate }>`: the forward direction, using exactly the line formula in `computeTotals` (`vat = roundVnd(net * p / 100)`).
- Use only `VatRate` / `VAT_RATES` (`packages/core/src/einvoice/schema.ts`) and `roundVnd` / `vatPercent` from `totals.ts`. Add no new rates.
- Errors:
  - `INVALID_AMOUNT` for a non-finite, negative or non-integer amount, with a hint;
  - `INVALID_VAT_RATE` for a rate not in `VAT_RATES`, with a hint listing them;
  - non-number input returns an error instead of throwing.
- Rounding: putting the leftover đồng in the VAT (net rounded half away from zero, VAT = gross − net) is this library's convention. No legal rule is cited for it. Document it as a convention in the JSDoc, `skills/vn-einvoice/SKILL.md` and `skills/vn-einvoice/references/` if a fitting file exists. Do not present it as a legal requirement.
- CLI: `vn-skills einvoice vat <amount> --rate <0|5|8|10|KCT|KKKNT> [--inclusive]`. Without `--inclusive` it applies VAT; with it, it splits. JSON output when piped.
- MCP: `vn_einvoice_vat` with `{ amount, rate, inclusive?: boolean }`, carrying the same title and read-only/closed-world annotations as the other tools.

## Acceptance
- [ ] ≥ 20 tests in `tests/einvoice-vat.test.ts`, covering:
  - 1 080 000 @8 inclusive → net 1 000 000, VAT 80 000;
  - 110 000 @10 → 100 000 + 10 000;
  - 100 000 @8 → net 92 593, VAT 7 407;
  - KCT, KKKNT and 0;
  - amount 0;
  - invalid rate, negative, fractional and string input;
  - a large amount;
  - `applyVat` agrees with `computeTotals` on a one-line invoice;
  - `net + vat === gross` for a range of amounts and rates;
  - CLI and MCP calls.
- [ ] Pure input → output cases are also added to `tests/golden/` (an `einvoice` golden file if one exists, else a new one loaded through `tests/golden.ts`).
- [ ] `skills/vn-einvoice/SKILL.md` describes the command, with trigger words such as "giá đã gồm VAT", "tách thuế VAT" and "giá chưa VAT". `tests/golden/triggers.json` is updated if it lists einvoice keywords.
- [ ] The README MCP tool table and tool count are updated in `README.md` and `README.vi.md`, and `tests/mcp.test.ts` / `tests/readme.test.ts` still pass.
- [ ] `pnpm build && pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm exec vitest run && pnpm format:check` pass.

